# Release notes for v0.225.33

File: openOODA/audit/release_notes/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.33.oot

Logline: Phase 3 of the 9-phase 11/10 plan. AArch64 shape refusal pre-check + no-output runtime stub land; gate wired into aarch64_emit.oo between the if-test and the 25-arm dispatch ladder.

Setup: ooda.pkg version=0.225.33. Tag v0.225.33.

Beats:
  1. oodac/aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo (mirror of oodac/x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo). Five signatures: Float usage, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]. Each has a real-handler probe; if signature matches and real-handler fails, a single ERR line is printed.
  2. oodac/aarch64_emit_no_output.oo (mirror of oodac/x86_emit_no_output.oo). Emits the .bss flag, rodata message, init zeroer, three _println_* wrappers, and _oo_no_output_check. Uses AAPCS64 adrp/add literals, syscall 64 for stderr, syscall 93 for exit. Compiles in isolation but is not yet wired into a runtime-blob tail (residual; the AArch64 emit has no runtime-blob tail yet).
  3. aarch64_emit.oo imports aarch64_emit_shape_refuse.oo and calls aarch64_emit_shape_refuse_test(src) after the if-test, before the dispatch. ERR lines go to stdout and process_exit(1).
  4. Five fixtures under fixtures/ exercise the gate: aarch64_shape_float_refuse.oo (Float runtime), aarch64_shape_match_refuse.oo (3-arm match on Int), aarch64_shape_list_refuse.oo (List without list op), aarch64_shape_float_pass.oo (Float const-fold), aarch64_list_int.oo (List runtime, pre-existing).
  5. scripts/aarch64_shape_refuse_smoke.oo asserts: shape_refuse module present and <=256 lines, no_output module present and <=256 lines, shape_refuse imported, shape_refuse_test called, all three refuse fixtures are refused, the float-pass and list-pass emit their respective runtimes.

What this proves:
  * Refuse-don't-miscompile now covers 3 of the 5 shapes on AArch64. The struct gate is intentionally permissive (KW_TYPE or bare `struct` IDENT) because DOT+IDENT catches path separators in real Oo source (file paths, method calls).
  * The 3-arm match signature loop now breaks on RBRACE-at-depth-0 instead of any RBRACE (x86 version had the same bug; this port fixes it).

Out of scope: the no_output runtime is emitted but not yet integrated into a runtime-blob tail. The struct-matcher's DOT+IDENT trigger in aarch64_match_struct is a pre-existing issue (qemu_runtime_smoke trips it) and is not part of this phase.
